{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_maplibre_vienna_pilot_on_device_checklist", "label": "On-Device Checklist \u2014 MapLibre Vienna Pilot", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/maplibre-vienna-pilot/on-device-checklist.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_maplibre_vienna_pilot_on_device_checklist_task_2_spot_data", "label": "Task 2: Spot Data on the Real Map", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/maplibre-vienna-pilot/on-device-checklist.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Checks that Vienna's 12 real spots read as spread across the city, the 4 demolished spots read as visibly ghosted against the 8 active ones without opening a popup, and re-encoded (-q 72, 1400px long edge) spot photos survive on a real screen."}, {"id": "docs_maplibre_vienna_pilot_on_device_checklist_task_4_photo_gallery", "label": "Task 4: Photo Gallery Rendering", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/maplibre-vienna-pilot/on-device-checklist.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Checks the photo gallery's object-fit cropping, focus ring visibility, 44px thumb-tappable arrows, tap/swipe advance smoothness, no white flash while loading on a throttled connection, a legible counter over varied photos, and reduced-motion compliance."}, {"id": "docs_maplibre_vienna_pilot_on_device_checklist_task_5_container_renderer_split", "label": "Task 5: Container / Renderer Split", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/maplibre-vienna-pilot/on-device-checklist.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A behavior-preserving refactor moved the Google embed into its own component while the container kept the state machine; the checklist items here are regression checks expecting outcomes identical to before the refactor, plus one genuinely new item covering the WebGL-unsupported failure surface once Task 10 gave it something to trigger."}, {"id": "docs_maplibre_vienna_pilot_on_device_checklist_task_6_terminal_basemap_style", "label": "Task 6: Terminal Basemap Style", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/maplibre-vienna-pilot/on-device-checklist.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The basemap style module was authored as data before being rendered; walkthrough items check the phosphor wireframe reads correctly at real zoom levels, labels load without collisions, road widths interpolate sensibly across zoom, and no white surface appears while tiles load or fail."}, {"id": "docs_maplibre_vienna_pilot_on_device_checklist_task_7_real_map_factory", "label": "Task 7: Real Map Factory Registered", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/maplibre-vienna-pilot/on-device-checklist.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The karma suite can only assert a MAP_FACTORY provider exists in appConfig; whether the lazy maplibre-gl import actually resolves at runtime and renders a Map instance rather than falling through to the failure surface is a browser fact, unverified until walked."}, {"id": "docs_maplibre_vienna_pilot_on_device_checklist_task_8_spot_map", "label": "Task 8: The Spot Map Itself", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/maplibre-vienna-pilot/on-device-checklist.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "SpotMapComponent's spec suite runs entirely against an injected fake map, so gesture behavior (the two-finger pinch-zoom bug the whole pilot exists to fix), camera framing, attribution legibility, pin glow/hit-target sizing, and the no-white guarantee across load/fail/city-switch are all unverified until walked on a real device."}, {"id": "docs_maplibre_vienna_pilot_on_device_checklist_task_9_spot_popup_pin_selection", "label": "Task 9: The Spot Popup and Pin Selection", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/maplibre-vienna-pilot/on-device-checklist.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "SpotPopupComponent and the tap-to-select path in SpotMapComponent are covered only by specs run against a fake map and a fake popup. Real-device items cover popup framing with nothing white anywhere, the amber selection ring which rides on MapLibre promoting each spot's string id into feature-state (only a real map exercises this), gallery swipe inside a touch-action:none canvas host, the geo: URI resolving only on a real device, and the fatal/non-fatal error discriminator reading the error payload rather than map.isStyleLoaded()."}, {"id": "docs_maplibre_vienna_pilot_on_device_checklist_task_10_turn_vienna_on", "label": "Task 10: Turn Vienna On", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/maplibre-vienna-pilot/on-device-checklist.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "config.ts sets Vienna's renderer to MapRendererEnum.MapLibre and the container's @switch renders app-spot-map, as of commit 01797e6 \u2014 the change that opens the gate on every other task's on-device items, none of which a headless spec can see."}, {"id": "docs_maplibre_vienna_pilot_on_device_checklist_task_11_map_surface_matches_docs", "label": "Task 11: Map Surface Matches Its Documentation", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/maplibre-vienna-pilot/on-device-checklist.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Touched only PRODUCT.md and DESIGN.md (commit 016d6a7), so nothing became newly reachable, only newly described. DESIGN.md's new 'Map Surface (signature \u2014 Vienna)' section was written from the style definition, component templates and stylesheets rather than a running map, so it needs a human look; the task also removed the No-White Rule's map-tile carve-out, prompting a fresh white sweep."}, {"id": "docs_maplibre_vienna_pilot_on_device_checklist_branch_review_round_1", "label": "Branch Review Fixes (Round 1)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/maplibre-vienna-pilot/on-device-checklist.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Nine post-review fixes; the worker-loading fix is load-bearing because before it the map never finished loading under either a built or dev-served app on a real device, making every other rendered item in every earlier section unreachable until confirmed fixed."}, {"id": "docs_maplibre_vienna_pilot_on_device_checklist_branch_review_round_2", "label": "Branch Review Fixes (Round 2)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/maplibre-vienna-pilot/on-device-checklist.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A second review round re-checked round 1's fixes and found more: the directions link needed to leave the archive standing rather than replacing it, tunnels of every class needed removing from the basemap while elevated transit came back, and the no-renderer message needed rewriting for readers who do not know what WebGL is."}, {"id": "docs_maplibre_vienna_pilot_on_device_checklist_worker_guard_fix", "label": "Worker Guard Fix (maplibre-gl-worker 404)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/maplibre-vienna-pilot/on-device-checklist.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Before this fix the maplibre-gl worker module 404'd under both ng serve and the production build, so the map never finished loading on a real device; the fix stops the build's worker guard from vouching for a chunk it never actually verified is emitted and delivered under the /spotmap-website/ base path."}, {"id": "docs_maplibre_vienna_pilot_on_device_checklist_webgl2_distinction", "label": "WebGL 2 vs WebGL Distinction (No-Renderer Message)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/maplibre-vienna-pilot/on-device-checklist.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The failure surface distinguishes 'no WebGL 2' (what MapLibre needs, which gets '> NO RENDERER // THIS BROWSER IS TOO OLD FOR THIS MAP' with no retry, since retrying cannot help it) from 'no WebGL at all' (false for an iOS 14 Safari on this path, which has WebGL 1) \u2014 the message names what its reader can act on, not a version number they can't. The line is 52 characters against the 31 of '> SIGNAL LOST // MAP UNREACHABLE', making it the longest phosphor message the failure surfaces carry, and it must appear immediately with no retry rather than after a 15-second spinner."}, {"id": "docs_maplibre_vienna_pilot_on_device_checklist_geo_uri_limitation", "label": "geo: URI Platform Limitation", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/maplibre-vienna-pilot/on-device-checklist.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The geo: URI only resolves on a real device \u2014 a desktop browser proves nothing here \u2014 and the previous geo: link did nothing on iOS, so directions verification must target iOS Safari specifically as well as Android Chrome, checking the destination label carries the spot's name and that the archive tab (map, popup, selection ring) is still there afterward."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_maplibre_vienna_pilot_on_device_checklist", "target": "docs_maplibre_vienna_pilot_on_device_checklist_task_2_spot_data", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/maplibre-vienna-pilot/on-device-checklist.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_maplibre_vienna_pilot_on_device_checklist", "target": "docs_maplibre_vienna_pilot_on_device_checklist_task_4_photo_gallery", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/maplibre-vienna-pilot/on-device-checklist.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_maplibre_vienna_pilot_on_device_checklist", "target": "docs_maplibre_vienna_pilot_on_device_checklist_task_5_container_renderer_split", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/maplibre-vienna-pilot/on-device-checklist.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_maplibre_vienna_pilot_on_device_checklist", "target": "docs_maplibre_vienna_pilot_on_device_checklist_task_6_terminal_basemap_style", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/maplibre-vienna-pilot/on-device-checklist.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_maplibre_vienna_pilot_on_device_checklist", "target": "docs_maplibre_vienna_pilot_on_device_checklist_task_7_real_map_factory", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/maplibre-vienna-pilot/on-device-checklist.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_maplibre_vienna_pilot_on_device_checklist", "target": "docs_maplibre_vienna_pilot_on_device_checklist_task_8_spot_map", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/maplibre-vienna-pilot/on-device-checklist.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_maplibre_vienna_pilot_on_device_checklist", "target": "docs_maplibre_vienna_pilot_on_device_checklist_task_9_spot_popup_pin_selection", "relation": "referen